         <title><![CDATA[Jays tickets, drums and Tinder: Hundreds of purchases made with city credit cards raise questions about misuse]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/toronto-city-hall-credit-cards-expenses-9.7437567?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/6517c435-2e77-4fc8-8232-c56a32508776,1795720246658/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C4500%2C2531%29%3B' alt='A close up of a woman&apos;s hand, holding a credit card in front of a laptop.' width='620' height='349' title='Hands holding plastic credit card and using laptop. Online shopping concept. Toned picture; Shutterstock ID 367136834'/><p>City of Toronto employees used city credit cards to make hundreds of purchases that included Blue Jays tickets, gift cards and later-disputed purchases on Tinder, an analysis of expenditure data by CBC News has found. The city says it has layers of oversight, but experts say it needs to be better.</p>]]></description>
